      "title": "Mahadev betting syndicate ‘kingpin’ extradited from Oman",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/mahadev-betting-app-kingpin-sourabh-chandrakar-extradited-from-oman-to-india/article71653674.ece",
      "description": "CBI says it secured extradition of Sourabh Chandrakar, who had been arrested by police in Oman following an Interpol Red Corner Notice",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-01T16:15:42"
    },
    {
      "title": "CBI extradites kingpin in ₹6,000-crore Mahadev betting app case from Oman",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cbi-extradites-kingpin-in-6-000-crore-mahadev-betting-app-case-from-oman-126110100742_1.html",
      "description": "The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) has extradited the alleged kingpin in the Rs 6,000-crore Mahadev online betting app case, Sourabh Chandrakar, from Oman, officials said on Sunday.\nA CBI team deputed to Oman has escorted Chandrakar back to India. He will now be produced before a special court in Raipur, Chhattisgarh, on Monday, they said.\nChandrakar was wanted in two CBI cases and one Enforcement Directorate (ED) case in which chargesheets have already been filed, a CBI spokesperson said in a statement.\n\"Based on the Red Corner Notice issued against Sourabh Chandrakar, he was located and detained by the Royal Oman Police,\" the official said.\nFollowing the information received from Muscat, the CBI and the ED immediately sent formal extradition proposals to the Sultanate of Oman, along with all the evidence gathered against the accused.\n\"The extradition request was pursued in close coordination with the agencies of the Government of India and the Interpol National Central ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T15:14:42"
    }
  ]
